# Local env files must never be uploaded.
#
# This is not belt-and-braces, it is the actual bug: when a `.vercelignore`
# exists the Vercel CLI uses it *instead of* `.gitignore`, so adding this file
# for the reason below silently removed the protection `.gitignore` was
# providing. `vercel deploy` then uploaded the developer's `.env`, Vite read it
# at build time as it would locally, and inlined `VITE_API_TOKEN` into
# `dist/assets/index-*.js` — publishing on a public URL the exact credential
# the proxy in `api/graphql.ts` exists to keep out of the bundle.
#
# `vercel.json` also pins `VITE_API_TOKEN` to an empty string at build time, so
# neither of these alone is load-bearing. A credential deserves both.
.env
.env.*
.vercel

# Vercel turns every file under `api/` into a deployed function, so a colocated
# test would become a public endpoint that imports Vitest. This repo keeps a test
# beside its subject, so the file is excluded from the upload rather than moved
# somewhere it does not belong.
api/*.test.ts
